intain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/28470","html_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/28470","diff_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/28470.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/28470.patch","merged_at":"2024-04-23T15:23:45Z"},"body":"Problem: `vim.deprecate()` can be relatively significantly slower than\r\n  the deprecated function in \"Nvim\" plugin.\r\nSolution: Optimize checks for \"Nvim\" plugin. This also results into not\r\n  distinguishing \"xxx-dev\" and \"xxx\" versions when doing checks, which\r\n  is essentially covered by the deprecation logic itself.\r\n\r\nResolve #28459.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nWith this rewrite I get the times from #28459: `{ 0.024827, 0.003797, 0.002024, 0.001774, 0.001703 }`.\r\nFor quicker reference:\r\n    -  On current Nightly it is something like `{ 3.72243, 0.918169, 0.968143, 0.763256, 0.783424 }`.\r\n    - On 0.9.5: `{ 0.002955, 0.000361, 0.000281, 0.000251, 0.00019 }`.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nIf these changes are too much, another approach might be to treat `vim.tbl_islist()` as a special case and use custom logic there instead of `vim.deprecate()`. Something along the lines of `if vim.fn.has('nvim-0.11') == 1 then ...`, etc.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/28470/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/28470/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":12577551298,"node_id":"REFE_lADOAPphoM6GgpV-zwAAAALtrjPC","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/events/12577551298","actor":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk"